//! Qu tree-walking interpreter -- milestone M2.
//!
//! Runs the *runnable subset* of Qu: scalars (`f64`), booleans, strings, and
//! 1-D real vectors (the shape signals live in), with ranges, element-wise
//! broadcasting, a DSP/stats-flavored builtin set, `for`/`while`/`if`, and
//! `print` with `{expr}` / `{expr:.3f}` interpolation. Matrices parse but do
//! not yet evaluate (a clear error is raised); they arrive with the linear
//! algebra milestone.
//!
//! This is the reference semantics -- deliberately simple and dependency-free.
//! `:=` is evaluated eagerly here (the fusing dataflow planner is a later
//! milestone); the distinction is preserved in the AST for when it lands.
//!
//! Determinism: `randn`/`rand` use a small splitmix64-based PRNG seeded from an
//! explicit `seed=` argument (or a fixed default), so runs reproduce exactly --
//! the reliability discipline the language asks for.

use qu_syntax::{parse, parse_expr, Arg, Expr, Idx, FnBody, ImportSource, Param, Program, ReduceOp, Reduction, Stmt, TypeTag, TYPE_TAGS};
